  "id": "unusual-sessions",
  "title": "Unusual Sessions",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "caeeb742-da37-4201-8fe2-cb3dee58c777",
      "question": "Using 2025 as the baseline, which 10 sessions from January 2 through March 12, 2026 were the most unusual among the 50 most liquid US stocks, and which features made each one unusual? Anomaly scores are neither forecasts nor explanations.",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T21:39:31.688184Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T21:39:45.761849Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Using 2025 as the baseline, here are the 10 most unusual sessions from January 2 through March 12, 2026 among the 50 most liquid US stocks:\n\n| Rank | Date | Ticker | Anomaly Score | Percentile | Key Features Making It Unusual (robust z-scores vs. 2025 baseline) |\n|------|------|--------|---------------|------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1 | 2026-02-25 | CRCL | 4.57 | 100.0 | **1-day return +21.7σ**, 5-day return +7.5σ, 20-day volatility +8.1σ, volume +5.0σ |\n| 2 | 2026-02-06 | CRWV | 2.70 | 99.96 | **1-day return +12.4σ**, 20-day volatility +6.0σ, volume +0.8σ |\n| 3 | 2026-02-06 | BMNR | 2.59 | 99.92 | **1-day return +10.8σ**, 20-day volatility +5.4σ, volume +2.2σ |\n| 4 | 2026-02-13 | COIN | 1.58 | 99.88 | **1-day return +10.3σ**, 20-day volatility +4.9σ, volume +2.7σ |\n| 5 | 2026-02-06 | COIN | 1.42 | 99.83 | **1-day return +8.3σ**, 20-day volatility +3.4σ, volume +1.8σ |\n| 6 | 2026-02-06 | CRCL | 1.41 | 99.79 | **1-day return +8.5σ**, 20-day volatility +3.7σ, volume +1.3σ |\n| 7 | 2026-02-09 | APP | 1.41 | 99.75 | **1-day return +8.4σ**, 20-day volatility +5.6σ, volume +1.4σ |\n| 8 | 2026-01-27 | UNH | 1.36 | 99.71 | **1-day return –12.3σ**, volume +7.7σ, 20-day volatility +3.0σ |\n| 9 | 2026-01-02 | BMNR | 1.26 | 99.67 | **1-day return +9.3σ**, 20-day volatility +5.2σ, volume +1.3σ |\n| 10 | 2026-02-12 | APP | 1.23 | 99.63 | **1-day return –12.9σ**, 20-day volatility +6.7σ, volume +2.9σ |\n\n**Features monitored:** The model tracks four daily features per asset: 1-day adjusted return, 5-day adjusted return, 20-day realized volatility, and 20-day log volume deviation. The \"observed deviations\" shown are robust z-scores measuring how many standard deviations each feature departed from its 2025 distribution—**not** returns or percentages themselves.\n\n**Limitations:** Anomaly scores describe unusual observed feature combinations; they are not forecasts or probabilities. The deviations are descriptive reason codes and do not establish a cause or adverse event. [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market anomaly scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:b42c6d6e384e099cce88459df00b72a30887f62eeb034d736f7c72e98cda1c81`",
